{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratumVanishes","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratumVanishes","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCapDerived"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.selfConjugate_two_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.selfConjugate_two_two","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SelfConjugateStratumVanishes.lean#L149-L155","doc":"`(2,2)` is self-conjugate, has column length two, and has four cells. It\nis therefore an **extremal** witness for `card_le_four_…`: the bound is\nattained and cannot be lowered to three, so that theorem is a statement about\na nonempty class rather than a vacuous one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.box2_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.box2_card","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SelfConjugateStratumVanishes.lean#L147-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.box2_colLen_le_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.box2_colLen_le_two","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SelfConjugateStratumVanishes.lean#L140-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.box2_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.box2_transpose","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SelfConjugateStratumVanishes.lean#L136-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.box2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.box2","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SelfConjugateStratumVanishes.lean#L127-L134","doc":"The `2 × 2` box — the diagram `(2,2)`, written as the box it is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.massWeight_eq_zero_of_selfConjugate_of_five_le_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.massWeight_eq_zero_of_selfConjugate_of_five_le_card","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SelfConjugateStratumVanishes.lean#L110-L123","doc":"**The mass-channel statement.** For `n ≥ 5`, a self-conjugate diagram\ncarries weight exactly zero — so the self-conjugate stratum of `∑_λ y_λ · χ_λ`\ncontributes nothing at all. This is the probe's `selfconj_share = 0.0000` at\n`n = 6, 9, 12`, and it holds for every `n ≥ 5`, not just those three. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.not_selfConjugate_of_colLen_le_two_of_five_le_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.not_selfConjugate_of_colLen_le_two_of_five_le_card","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SelfConjugateStratumVanishes.lean#L101-L108","doc":"Contrapositive, in the form the Wedderburn sums consume: past four cells a\ntwo-row diagram is **never** self-conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.card_le_four_of_selfConjugate_of_colLen_le_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.card_le_four_of_selfConjugate_of_colLen_le_two","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SelfConjugateStratumVanishes.lean#L88-L99","doc":"**Main bound.** A self-conjugate diagram surviving the two-row cap has at\nmost four cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.cell_lt_two_of_selfConjugate_of_colLen_le_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.cell_lt_two_of_selfConjugate_of_colLen_le_two","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SelfConjugateStratumVanishes.lean#L68-L86","doc":"A self-conjugate diagram capped at two rows sits inside the `2 × 2` box:\nevery cell has both coordinates `< 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.rowLen_zero_eq_colLen_zero_of_selfConjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.SelfConjugateStratum.rowLen_zero_eq_colLen_zero_of_selfConjugate","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/SelfConjugateStratumVanishes.lean#L60-L66","doc":"A self-conjugate diagram has equal first row and first column lengths.\n`μ.transpose.rowLen 0 = μ.colLen 0` always; self-conjugacy rewrites the left. ","signatureChunk":0}]}